# Load-bearing exclusions. Adding a fixture or testdata directory means adding
# it here in the SAME commit, or the format job starts rewriting test inputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Test fixtures and goldens. The hook tests compare these byte for byte, and
# several payloads are malformed JSON ON PURPOSE — prettier errors on those
# rather than warning, so a check run over them can never go green.
hooks/go/**/testdata/
hooks/go/surfaces/*/payloads/
# The TypeScript conformance goldens are compared byte for byte.
.github/tools/src/conformance/testing/fixtures/

evals/runs/

# Work artifacts retain their approved content and flow bindings.
docs/specs/

# Committed hook binaries.
hooks/bin/

# Not ours.
.git/
node_modules/

# npm generates this with its own 2-space style; prettier would fight it.
package-lock.json

# husky runtime shims, generated by `npm install` (prepare script).
.github/husky/_/

.github/workflows/release.lock.yml
.github/workflows/backlog-grooming.lock.yml
.github/aw/actions-lock.json

